You convert one research hypothesis on ageing into a structured card. Record only what the text states. You are a parser, not a scientist: add no facts, no evidence, no judgements.

Hypothesis text:
<<<TEXT
{{ text }}
TEXT>>>

Fields:
- hypothesis_type: interventional (an intervention changes an outcome) | mechanistic (explains how or why an effect happens) | biomarker (a marker predicts an outcome) | observational (an exposure or variant is associated with an outcome).
- claim_plain: one plain sentence, no jargon: what is proposed and what it should lead to.
- pico: population {taxon (NCBITaxon id if obvious, else omit), label, strain, sex, age, age_at_start}; intervention: list of {type: compound|gene|diet|procedure|other, label, regimen} (one item, or several for a combination); comparator {type: placebo|untreated|standard_care|wild_type|monotherapy|active_drug|chronological_age|other, label}; outcome {endpoint: lifespan|healthspan|biomarker|disease|mechanism|unknown, metric}; time. Write "unknown" for anything the text does not state. Never fill a missing population, species or endpoint from background knowledge.
- claims: 1 to 8 atomic claims. Each: id (c1, c2, ...), subject {label}, relation, object {label, hallmark (optional)}, qualifiers (species, strain, sex, tissue, dose, age_at_start, comparator, direction, measure: only those the text states), role, source_span.
  - relation, closed list: {{ relations }}. If nothing fits, use "other" and add "note".
  - role: premise | mechanism | analog | outcome | translation. Exactly one claim has role "outcome": the main claim of the hypothesis.
  - Atomic: one relation and one context per claim. "inhibits X and reduces Y" gives two claims; "in mice and flies" gives two claims. A mechanism chain is several claims linked by "requires" edges. A step from one species to another is its own claim (role translation).
  - source_span: copy the exact words of the text this claim comes from, character for character (a fragment of the text above, not a paraphrase). A claim the text does not state is not allowed.
  - hallmark (optional) is one of: {{ hallmarks }}.
- edges: list of {from, to, type: requires|supports_if_true|analog_of|contradicts} between claim ids.
- declared_novelty: what the text says is new, else "unknown".
- decisive_experiment: {system: cells|worm|fly|yeast|mouse|rat|human|data_analysis|unknown, endpoint, duration_class: weeks|months|years|decades|unknown}: the experiment that would settle the outcome claim, as far as the text defines it.
- declared_alternatives, declared_decision_criteria: only if the text states them, else [] and "unknown".
- risks: risks the text names, else [].

